<%#
  Optional connections to outside systems - off by default, unlike SSO_MODE
  sign-in which this has nothing to do with. Azure Entra ID Directory is the
  first (and for now only) one: a cached name/email pull (Sync now, below),
  plus the live search that powers Person and Group fields on any entity
  type - both gated by this one toggle, since both reuse the same app
  registration and app-only token.
%>
<div id="integrationsSettings">
  <p class="text-muted small">
    Optional connections MyWork can use. Nothing here is required, and each is
    off until you turn it on.
  </p>

  <div class="card" style="max-width: 40rem;">
    <div class="card-body">
      <div class="d-flex align-items-center justify-content-between">
        <h6 class="card-title mb-1"><i class="bi bi-microsoft"></i> Azure Entra ID Directory</h6>
        <div class="form-check form-switch mb-0">
          <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="entraDirectoryEnabled" disabled>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="card-text text-muted small">
        Pulls a list of names and email addresses from your organization's
        Entra directory (Sync now, below), and powers the live search box on
        any <strong>Person</strong> or <strong>Group</strong> field you add to
        an entity type in Settings &gt; Entity Types. Reuses the same Azure app
        registration as single sign-on - it needs the
        <code>User.Read.All</code> and <code>Group.Read.All</code> application
        permissions, with admin consent, added to that app registration.
      </p>

      <div id="entraDirectoryStatus" class="small mb-2"></div>

      <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success" id="entraDirectorySyncBtn" disabled>
          <i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat"></i> Sync now
        </button>
        <span class="text-muted small" id="entraDirectorySyncedAt"></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="/js/settings-integrations.js"></script>
